Reducing `SPLIT_K` to 16 cuts atomic contention per output element by 4x while still producing 1024 total program instances (`grid_m * SPLIT_K = 64 * 16`), which is more than enough concurrent work to fully occupy the GPU's SMs and hide memory latency for the large K-dimension reduction. This is a legitimate split-K tuning optimization (balancing atomic overhead vs. parallelism), not just an arbitrary launch-parameter tweak.

