- Implement the complete `forward()` computation with exactly one custom
  Triton kernel. Fuse operations that appear in the reference when needed.
- Launch Triton normally with `custom_kernel[grid](...)`; Triton will enqueue
  work on PyTorch's current CUDA stream. Do not synchronize in `forward()`.
- Define `validate_generated_code()` and make one representative kernel launch
  from it so compile validation catches Triton JIT/compiler errors before
  correctness testing. Do not benchmark or autotune in this hook; the framework
  synchronizes after calling it.
