node 3_20260823-210328 codegen_edits llm_response: Looking at this kernel, it's already a cooperative, spatially-tiled depthwise convolution (2D output tiling with vectorized loads). Since KH=3 must be padded to BLOCK_KH=4 (power-of-2 requirement for `tl.arange`), the kernel materializes an unnecessary 3D `(BLOCK_KH, BLOCK_OH, BLOCK_OW)` tensor, wasting 25% of lanes/registers on a fully-masked, useless kh=3 slice, and inflates register pressure for address/mask computation. Since `KH` is a compile-time constant, I replace the vectorized-over-kh 3D tensor approach with a `tl.static_range` unrolled loop that accumulates over exactly `KH` iterations using compact 2D `(BLOCK_OH, BLOCK_OW)` tiles per iteration — eliminating the padded/masked-out kh lane and cutting per-program register/index-computation overhead (register/tensor blocking improvement), while preserving identical numerics and memory access patterns.

